      "topic": {
        "text": "Execution of a Java for loop",
        "refs": ["Q0002"]
      },
      "explanation_text": {
        "text": "When Java encounters a for loop it first executes the initialization statement (e.g., initializing I to zero), then evaluates the loop condition; if the condition is true the loop body is executed, after which the update expression increments the counter, and the process repeats until the condition becomes false.",
        "refs": ["Q0002", "Q0003", "Q0004"]
      },
      "explanation_type": null
    }
  ],
  "examples": [],
  "facts": [
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "Loop counter variables are commonly named I, J, or K.",
        "refs": ["Q0001"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "A for loop can be written without braces if it contains a single statement.",
        "refs": ["Q0002"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "If the loop counter is initialized to zero, using the less‑than operator (<) will execute the loop the desired number of times; alternatively, initializing to one and using less‑than‑or‑equal (≤) works as well.",
        "refs": ["Q0004"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    }
  ],
  "formulas": [],
  "procedures": [
    {
      "procedure_name": {
        "text": "Steps of a Java for loop",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "steps": [
        {
          "text": "Declare and initialize a loop counter variable (e.g., int I = 0).",
          "refs": ["Q0000"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Write a boolean condition that determines loop continuation (e.g., I < 5).",
          "refs": ["Q0001"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Provide an update expression to modify the counter after each iteration (e.g., I++).",
          "refs": ["Q0001"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Place the loop body statements to be repeated.",
          "refs": ["Q0001"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Execute: initialize counter, evaluate condition, run body, apply update, repeat until condition is false.",
          "refs": ["Q0002", "Q0003", "Q0004"]
        }
      ],
      "prerequisites": null,
      "outcomes": null,
      "content": {
        "text": "A for loop repeats a block of code a specified number of times according to its initialization, condition, and update components.",
        "refs": ["Q0000", "Q0001"]
      }
    }
